Z||000011||stimpy||10-04-2001||06:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>Actually Eagle was around before Chrysler... but as a model, not a make.  The AMC Eagle was a car.  After Chrysler bought out AMC they decided to name the new division Eagle.<P>Also not all cars sold as Eagles were re-badged Mitsubishi's.  There was the Eagle Vision sedan which was a rebadged Dodge Intrepid.  Also the Eagle Premier which was a re-badged Dodge Monico (could this have been a Mitsu?  Was a horrible peace of garbage!).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here is an apparently little known fact. The Dodge Monaco and Eagle Premier were actually French. (Actually explains a lot.) The Renault R9 I believe was rebadged for sale at Dodge and Eagle dealerships, who also sold the notorious Renault Alliant.<BR>||||reg||1
