Z||000020||theogre||10-06-2001||12:51 PM||||Trivia... The AMC Eagle was a 4WD car in a small station wagon format. Most of the people I've known that had them really liked them. They were higher ground clearance than Subaru's 4WD cars at the time. (the Subaru's could be had 2 or 4wd. You could actually convert a 2wd to 4wd by changing the transmission and other easily bolted in parts. Took about a day to convert one if you knew how.)<P>AMC was always a mixed bag. For each product they did right 5 sucked. They took a real pounding on certain Jeep models over stability and other issues. I think it was CJ5 that got the worst of that. On the otherhand the Jeep Scrambler pickup truck style jeep sold rather well. Scrambler was always one of my favorites.<P>Eagle and Gremlin sold like crazy but Pacer looked to much like a rolling greenhouse and didn't sell all that well. Nobody could quite figure what to make of Pacer but it did have a huge interior for it's size and visiblity that was hard to beat. I believe it had more glass in it than any other car at that time. It also presented some difficult design issues. It was tought to shape some of those windows so you didn't get really weird distortions as you looked thru them. <P>As much as people joked about Gremlin, those cars could move rather well stock. Like Chevy Vega they were rather popular to stuff V8's into. Also like Vega and several others from Ford and GM, they were nose heavy and could spin out fairly easy if you didn't watch them.<P>PArt of AMC's problem was the way they did drive train systems. You'd have a motor from one company bolted to a tranny(and transfer case) from another and axles from someone else yet. But they were altered enough that many parts couldn't be transfered from the orignal source of the parts. It was really common to yank the motor/tranny/Tcase from jeep and put in a Ford or Chevy set. This allowed more engine choices but just as importantly you could now use very common and plentifull new/used parts to fix it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000021||Jimmy||10-06-2001||01:04 PM||||Jaei Sun meant that the cars in question were pretty much completely Japanese.  I think he was giving Yokle Sweet/Santa looser a little crap because is so ignorantly anti-asian.  <P>Believe me when I say Jaei Sun is a car guy.  He likes Fieros for the obvious reasons, he also loves other cars made in Europe and Japan(rightfully so). <P>Nice point Phil, I guess we should watch out for Mercedes, Porsche (German tanks), and VW (Hitler honored it by calling it the "Peoples Car").    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Jim <BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT<P>edited for spelling<p>[This message has been edited by Jimmy (edited 10-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||sloth85GT||10-06-2001||03:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jimmy:<BR><B>Jaei Sun meant that the cars in question were pretty much completely Japanese.  I think he was giving Yokle Sweet/Santa looser a little crap because is so ignorantly anti-asian.  <P>Believe me when I say Jaei Sun is a car guy.  He likes Fieros for the obvious reasons, he also loves other cars made in Europe and Japan(rightfully so). <P>Nice point Phil, I guess we should watch out for Mercedes, Porsche (German tanks), and VW (Hitler honored it by calling it the "Peoples Car").     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Jim <BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT<P>edited for spelling<P>[This message has been edited by Jimmy (edited 10-06-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It makes sense now. I used to be all anti-asian cars but now I still kinda am, but they do make some good stuff. I personall will only buy american, but I won't knock what other people have anymore.<BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000023||Jimmy||10-06-2001||03:48 PM||||No big deal if you don't like Asian or any kind of cars for that matter, I'm just saying we could do with a few less people that talk crap about cars they know nothing about.<P>I have friends that ride in my Fiero and know a lot about them and don't like them AT ALL.  No biggie its just people that say "those are POS" and direct at some vehicle they know nothing about.<P>/steps onto soapbox/<P>I know it seems silly to get worked up about a piece of metal(or plastic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ), but I think the way a person expresses their feelings(ignorance or hatred) about a car can show a lot about their character.  WHEW  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>/steps off of soapbox/ <P>and now to try and keep this post somewhat on topic....my girlfriend drives an Eagle Talon and its a Mitsu.<P>Jim<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT<BR>MSCF||||reg||1
